{"id":"000W1O","title":"Compressed Fog","author":"Jorava","solvedCount":20,"difficulty":1,"rating":"88 %","firstSeen":"2026-11-14T19:15:20+00:00","posted":"Heute, 17:22 Uhr","rules":"Compressed dynamic fog, killer cages, kropki.\n\nSolve in Sudokupad\n\nwafflefries introduced this concept in the puzzle Square Up! #1. It's an interesting idea, so I made my own spin on it.\n\n-----\n\nRules:\n\nNormal sudoku rules apply. Place the digits 1-9 in every row, column, and 3x3 box.\n\nKiller Cages:\nDigits in a cage cannot repeat, and must sum to the cage's number, if given.\n\nKropki:\nDigits paired by a black dot are in 1:2 ratio (one is double the other). Digits paired by a white dot are consecutive.\n\nDynamic Fog:\nMost of the grid and clues are hidden under fog. Placing correct digits may reveal some fog. All fog will be cleared by the end. Guessing is never required.\n\nCompressed Fog:\nIf two revealed cells only have fog-covered cells between them, the two cells are considered adjacent, and any clues partially hidden between the two revealed cells affects the digits in both cells. Once a clue has been fully revealed, it works normally.","solutionCode":"Row 1","tags":["Sudoku","Kropki","Killer (Variante)"],"links":[{"url":"https://sudokupad.app/hqxvie6uma","kind":"sudokupad"}],"data":"","error":null,"settings":{},"link":"https://sudokupad.app/hqxvie6uma","linkKind":"sudokupad","summary":{"format":"scl","decoded":true,"rows":9,"cols":9,"cages":8,"hasSolution":true,"features":["overlays"]},"attempts":0,"fetched":"2026-11-14T19:15:20+00:00"}